{
  "title": "Nursemaid's Elbow",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4012/nursemaids-elbow",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Aug 21 2022",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nursemaid's Elbow is a common injury of early childhood that results in subluxation of the annular ligament due to a sudden longitudinal traction applied to the hand.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made clinically with a child that holds the elbow in slight flexion with pain and tenderness localized to the lateral aspect of the elbow.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually closed reduction with either a supination or a hyperpronation technique.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common in children from **1 to 4 years of age**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**average age is 28 months**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**rare after 5 years of age**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "slightly more common in females",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism of injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**sudden, longitudinal traction applied to the hand with the elbow extended and forearm pronated**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may also be caused by a fall",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**annular ligament becomes interposed between radial head and capitellum**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4012/images/nursemaid%20elbow.jpg",
                      "caption": "shows nursemaid elbow"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "in children 5 years of age or older, subluxation is prevented by a thicker and stronger distal attachment of the annular ligament",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**a click may be heard** or felt by the person pulling the child's arm",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "child **refuses to use** the affected limb",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "holds the **elbow in slight flexion** and the forearm pronated",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical Exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain and **tenderness localized** to the lateral aspect of the elbow",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "range of motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "full flexion and extension",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "pain with supination",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**not required** in the setting of the classic presentation of",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "history of traction injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "child five years or younger",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "consistent clinical exam",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "when obtained, elbow **radiographs are normal**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**25% will show radiocapitellar line slightly lateral to center of capitellum**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ultrasound",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4012/images/nursemaid_ultrasound.jpg",
              "caption": "Ultrasound demonstrating nursemaid&#39;s elbow."
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "helpful for **confirming the diagnosis** when necessary",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "when the mechanism of injury is not evident",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "when physical examination is inconclusive",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "benefits",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "no radiation to the patient",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "can visualize soft tissues",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "increase echo-negative area between capitellum and radial head",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "sensitivity 64.9% and specificity 100%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nursemaid elbow is a diagnosis of exclusion",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Differential diagnosis of a painful elbow with limited supination",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "traumatic causes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "supracondylar fracture, olecranon fracture, radial neck fracture, lateral condyle fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "contusion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "infection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "septic arthritis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "congenital",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "radial head dislocation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "forearm synostosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "closed reduction of annular ligament subluxation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "for **majority of cases**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "must be certain no fracture is present prior to any manipulation",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open reduction rarely required",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "for chronic, symptomatic **subluxations that cannot be reduced**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Closed reduction of annular ligament subluxation**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**supination technique**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "while holding the arm supinated the elbow is then maximally flexed",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "the physician’s thumb applies pressure over the radial head and a palpable click is often heard with reduction of the radial head",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**hyperpronation technique**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "involves hyperpronation of the forearm while in the flexed position",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "followup",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "child should begin to use the arm within minutes after reduction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**immobilization is unnecessary after first episode**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Recurrence**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**may occur, especially** if the child is younger than 3 years",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "initially treat with cast application in flexion and neutral or supination",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Excellent when reduced in a timely manner",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
